// Breaks every live brick the ball overlaps, scores it, and bounces the ball
// out of the overlap: the axis with the smallest penetration is the face that
// was hit. At most ONE bounce per axis per pass: on a grid seam (gap 8 px <
// ball diameter 14 px) the ball overlaps two bricks in the same pass, and a
// per-brick `vy = -vy` would invert twice and cancel out. Returns true when at
// least one brick was resolved.
